; Every dependency of this package is public, and this file says so out loud
; rather than leaving it to whatever registry the machine happens to be pointed
; at. That is not a preference: `npm install` writes a `resolved` URL per package
; into package-lock.json, so the configured registry is committed along with it.
; On a work machine the configured registry is a corporate mirror, and several
; hundred of its URLs reached this public repository once — an internal hostname
; published, and a CI that then timed out fetching from a host a GitHub runner
; has no way to resolve. The failure surfaced on one Node version as a plain
; ETIMEDOUT and on the other as "Exit handler never called!", which is a long
; way from the cause.
;
; This governs generation only. `npm ci` installs from the `resolved` URLs
; already in the lockfile, so a lockfile written somewhere else is not corrected
; by this file — scripts/hygiene.mjs is the half that catches that, and it runs
; in CI where no local config applies.
;
; npm never packs .npmrc into a published tarball, and "files" in package.json
; does not list it either, so nothing here ships.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
